formatted_question:
In the case report "Autoimmune heparin-induced thrombocytopenia following cardiac surgery", the authors note that some patients with atypical, often severe clinical courses due to HIT have antibodies with a particular platelet-activating behavior. What kind of platelet-activating properties do these HIT antibodies have?
(A) heparin-dependent platelet-activating properties;
(B) heparin-independent platelet-activating properties;
(C) Fc receptor–mediated platelet-aggregating effects only during ongoing UFH therapy;
(D) complement-mediated thrombotic microangiopathy–inducing properties;
(E) platelet factor 4–heparin complex–restricted binding properties;

